            <ArticleTitle>Recurrent histiocytosis X with mandibular lesions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>420-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 19-year old male patient suffered a recurrence of histiocytosis X after 11 years of apparent remission. Radiographic lesions were found in the mandible. Loose and painful teeth were present. Low-dose radiation to the mandible and oral chemotherapy were followed with regression of bony lesions. Reports of incidence, treatment methods, and recurrences are reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
